{{Term/Store|Boar|Boars|Series, BotW|plural}} are recurring [[Animal]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Name Ref}}

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}} and {{TotK|-}}===
{{BotW}} and {{TotK}} feature [[Woodland Boar]]s and [[Red-Tusked Boar]]s. They are commonly found in [[Forest]]s. When encountered, they will either flee from [[Link]] or charge at him in defense. When defeated, Woodland Boars drop [[Raw Meat]], while Red-Tusked Boars drop [[Raw Prime Meat]]. [[Bokoblin]]s will sometimes chase after Boars that wander near them, occasionally killing and eating them.

[[Statue]]s of Boars can be found around many of the [[Zonai Ruin]]s on the [[Surface]]. The [[Zonai]] used them to represent the [[Triforce of Power]].<ref name="CaC 342"/> Because of [[Demon King Ganondorf]]'s association with Boars, the people of Hyrule came to view them as evil. Many of the Boar Statues would end up being destroyed.<ref name="Zelda Notes"/>

==Other Appearances==
===Philips CD-i Games===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
In {{TFoE}} and {{TWoG}}, Boars appear as unnamed enemies. They are short, fast enemies that run in a linear path and will fall to a single sword hit. However, due to their small size, striking one may become difficult if [[Link]] or [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]] are even slightly on an incline. In {{TFoE|-}}, they can be found in the [[Harlequin Bazaar]]. In {{TWoG|-}}, they inhabit [[Aru Ainu]].
{{Noncanon|End}}

==Trivia==
* The beast form of [[Ganon]] tends to resemble a giant Boar.<ref name="Hyrule Historia 90"/>

